    "title": "Reality Steve Drops Taylor Frankie Paul’s ‘Bachelorette’ Winner—Reveals Whether They’re Still Together",
    "text": "‘Mormon Wives’ Taylor Frankie Paul & Mayci Neeley Debate Sexcations | If It Were Me | CosmopolitanCosmopolitan USLIVECurrent Time 0:00Total Duration 8:01Reality Steve revealed who won Taylor Frankie Paul’s season of The Bachelorette—and if they’re still together.The Bachelorette was just cancelled by ABC following a video of a 2023 incident involving Taylor and Dakota Mortensen.Taylor’s winner has spoken out on the show being pulled.The Bachelorette has been canceled, but as a reminder Taylor Frankie Paul filmed an entire season worth of content before ABC pulled the show, and she even got engaged. So, what happened? Reality Steve revealed which contestant Taylor ended with (before the season was cancelled), and where they stand now. According to the longtime Bachelor Nation spoiler sleuth, Taylor’s final four were Shane Parton, Lew Evans, Doug Mason, and Casey Hux. She then brought Shane, Lew, and Doug to Salt Lake City for Fantasy Suite dates, and Shane and Doug ended up being her final two. The winner?That’d be Doug Mason, who she got engaged to, and broke up with one month later.“Since filming ended, Taylor and Doug have broken up. And yes, it's because of Dakota,” Steve claimed in part, alleging that “Doug flew to Utah about a month after the engagement (in January I'm told), and Taylor ended it. The reasons behind it? I guess we'll find out when it airs, but if Taylor says it's anything other than Dakota, she's not being honest with herself or the audience.”Doug has since spoken out about The Bachelorette’s cancellation:",
